  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pennsylvania received $82.2M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Obligations fell 99.7% year over year. The state recorded 706 awards with an average award size of $116K. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the top buyer, obligating $75.5M so far in FY2027. OLYMPUS AMERICA INC is the largest vendor, receiving $19.2M in obligations. Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations, with $17.1M. Electric Power Distribution is the second largest industry, with $10.6M. FY22 through FY26 obligations show much higher annual totals, with FY26 at $24.9B and FY25 at $26.9B, highlighting that current-year totals are partial and reflect fiscal year to date activity. The data shows concentration by a few agencies and vendors in the current fiscal year to date period, and a mix of manufacturing and services among the top industries.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did obligations fall so sharply in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 99.7% year over year. The FY2027 to date total is $82.2M compared with prior full fiscal years that reached billions, for example FY26 at $24.9B and FY25 at $26.9B. The current-year total is partial, fiscal year to date. Current-year scope and timing explain why the FY2027 number is far smaller than prior full-year totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominated FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $75.5M, far more than any other agency in the state. The Department of Justice obligated $3.4M and the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $1.8M. OLYMPUS AMERICA INC received $19.2M and CONSTELLATION NEWENERGY, INC. received $10.2M among the top vendors."
      }
    ]
  },
